<h2>Who clear aligners work for</h2>
<p>Aligners are excellent for the most common adult cases: mild to moderate crowding, gaps, post-braces relapse, and rotated teeth. For severe bite issues or complex skeletal problems, traditional braces or an orthodontic referral may be a better fit — and we'll tell you up front if that's the case.</p>

<h2>How treatment works</h2>
<ol class="checklist" style="list-style:decimal;padding-left:28px">
  <li><strong>Digital scan.</strong> No goopy impressions — a quick digital scan of your teeth.</li>
  <li><strong>Treatment plan.</strong> You see a 3D simulation of how your teeth will move over time.</li>
  <li><strong>Aligners.</strong> Each clear tray moves your teeth a small, calibrated amount. You switch trays every 1–2 weeks.</li>
  <li><strong>Refinement.</strong> Most cases finish with a short refinement series to lock in the result.</li>
  <li><strong>Retainers.</strong> Lifetime nighttime retainer wear keeps your new alignment stable. This part is non-negotiable.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Combining with whitening or veneers</h2>
<p>Many patients align first, then whiten or place veneers — straight teeth take less restorative work and look better when finished. We'll lay out the right sequence at your consultation.</p>

<h2>Clear aligners vs. braces</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li><strong>Appearance:</strong> aligners are nearly invisible; braces are on your teeth for the whole treatment.</li>
  <li><strong>Eating and cleaning:</strong> aligners come out, so you eat normally and brush and floss as usual.</li>
  <li><strong>Responsibility:</strong> aligners only work when you wear them about 22 hours a day. Braces work whether you remember them or not.</li>
  <li><strong>Complex cases:</strong> severe bite or jaw problems are often better treated with braces by an orthodontist, and we'll tell you if that's the better route.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Comparing Invisalign and other clear aligners in Tempe</h2>
<p>If you've been researching Invisalign, you're in the right place to ask questions. Invisalign is one brand of clear aligner; we offer clear aligner treatment that works the same basic way. The brand matters less than the planning and supervision behind it: dentist-supervised aligners include an exam before you start, check-ins during treatment, and retainers to hold the result. Mail-order aligner programs offer far less in-person supervision, so problems can go unnoticed until late in treatment.</p>

<h2>What clear aligners cost</h2>
<p>We quote after your scan and exam so the price matches your actual case. You'll get it in writing before you start. See <a href="/insurance-financing/">insurance &amp; financing</a> for payment options; some dental plans include orthodontic benefits that can apply. Clear aligners are part of our <a href="/services/cosmetic-dentistry/">cosmetic dentistry</a> in Tempe, AZ.</p>
